## Class-
    definition- "class consist of state ans the behaviour of an object."
        - it encapsulate data and method in a single unit.
        - class doesn't alocate memory until an object is created.
        - an object can not exist without class but class can exist
           without any object.


properties = state = attributes
methods = behaviour of object

## advantages of OOP
- easy to reuse code
- hide complex details
- parent child relationship
- one method many uses
- simplify complex system
- DRY = do not repeat yourself

## disadvantages of OOP
- slower performance
- overcomplicating simple task
- hard to learn
- wastage of memory


